<description>&lt;p&gt;Intercommunal clashes in Lakes state, especially Rumbek, have escalated, prompting a curfew and a return of caretaker governor Rin Tueny to the area. United Nations Mission in South Sudan has increased civilian protection efforts after deadly violence in Rumbek, while two SSPDF soldiers were wounded in an attack on a Mundri West military outpost and the U.S. Embassy condemned an assault on WFP workers in Jonglei that involved looting of aid. A cleric of the AIC was shot dead in Juba and a Juba High Court sentenced five officers to 24 years for raiding a general's home. Pibor appealed to Jonglei authorities to return 81 abducted women and children. The lethal communal violence now far exceeds the two battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisAFBVV95cUxOTzV4TDJ2WUhwUEdhSi1DV2c1RkRSa2ZzV05DWXpzcjh3ZncwQ2w4ay1neloySU81WUxxX2owb1VNQXBPWXhHbWtBcXc3aDd0dUI0T0JWRUoyaHhWYmY5bWcwTFFrWXV5SFFKMFEwSnhNSWw5bWNIQVAzVE5SM081T3RxTXNYMkVXTkRUSldMU1VBWnlnbExOOExrX2lkVXNmSnd0V0JWdloyLUtiMTRoSw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Africanews English&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Africa.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiREFVX3lxTFBZV2l2WWEwN0hJeEVwNkVsaE9iVGFJZDY2VnAxQXRWbEI3Z0pzWWJnV195My0tbTZUN0ZtWE9FYnhaQXJi0gFKQVVfeXFMTmxyN0hCbzdqSGpsblBxa2pSYTljOXhpTlkzNE95aGQzZGpoU3dBc2U5VnJBSlYtTEZvd1dGbWlsbDlIOEJ3OUh3UkE?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxNajRneUIzNVQwRGtLeEtpSm9jOThWdFNWOEJqb0JaamxPQ2xtVUdWTExXQzZwbVllZ1c2UDhSWlg3Z2JxQlJ6b